From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:01:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: describe the QSPIMC boot NOR
 controller

The T8132 boot NOR (iBoot, NVRAM, syscfg) sits behind a QSPIMC at
0x3ad118000. Describe it, disabled, so boards can enable it.

Values (MEASURED, J604 runtime ADT /arm-io/qspi, saved 2026-11-04):
reg[0] 0x3ad118000 +0x4000 and reg[1] 0x3ad118800 +0x4000 (overlapping
P and C apertures, one 0x4800 resource), interrupts 0x424 = 1060,
compatible "qspi,qspimc". The power domain is the existing ps_qspi.
The 200 MHz input clock is the SoC value from Aurora's t8132.dtsi
(SOURCE c6b301adfd); the ADT gives only a clock id, so the rate is
TO-VERIFY against the driver's probe line on the J604.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index a3683307b5..d34dd727ec 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -381,6 +381,18 @@
 		clock-output-names = "clkref";
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * QSPIMC input clock. The ADT gives only a clock-id (0x194); the rate is
+	 * the T8132 SoC value Aurora's t8132.dtsi uses. The driver logs it at
+	 * probe and derives its divider from it.
+	 */
+	qspi_clk: clock-qspi {
+		compatible = "fixed-clock";
+		#clock-cells = <0>;
+		clock-frequency = <200000000>;
+		clock-output-names = "qspi";
+	};
+
 	soc: soc {
 		compatible = "simple-bus";
 		#address-cells = <2>;
@@ -391,6 +403,23 @@
 		/* Required to get >32-bit DMA via DARTs */
 		dma-ranges = <0 0 0 0 0xffffffff 0xffffc000>;
 
+		/*
+		 * Boot NOR controller. ADT /arm-io/qspi: P block 0x3ad118000 and
+		 * C block 0x3ad118800, each 0x4000 long and overlapping; one
+		 * resource covers both (the driver needs C + 0xa0). IRQ 1060.
+		 */
+		qspi: spi@3ad118000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t8132-qspi";
+			reg = <0x3 0xad118000 0 0x4800>;
+			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 1060 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			clocks = <&qspi_clk>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_qspi>;
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		cpufreq_e: performance-controller@210e20000 {
 			compatible = "apple,t8132-cluster-cpufreq", "apple,cluster-cpufreq";
 			reg = <0x2 0x10e20000 0 0x1000>;
